You will never be disintegrated for attempting to kill a priest in his
temple.  The priest can paralyse you (among other magic attacks), so free
action is very good to have, and his god will hit you with lightning, so
shock resistance is handy, and your wisdom will be abused, but you will
never be targeted by a divinely-fuelled disintegration attack purely
because you assaulted a priest.  Those are reserved for when a god
decides you must be expunged from reality for impudent prayer, and fails
to do so by smashing you with a lightning bolt.

(My single favorite piece of code in Nethack is the bit that gives you
experience for destroying a monster by praying inside it and incurring
divine wrath, as much for this comment as for the fact it happens:
	/* Yup, you get experience.  It takes guts to successfully
	 * pull off this trick on your god, anyway.
